description:
`detectors/apple.py` checks for `*.xcodeproj` / `*.xcworkspace` at the project root only:

\`\`\`python
def detect(project_dir: Path) -> dict | None:
    if any(project_dir.glob("*.xcodeproj")) or any(project_dir.glob("*.xcworkspace")):
        return {"archetypes": ["apple"]}
    return None
\`\`\`

This misses projects that nest their Xcode project a level or two down (e.g. `ios/MyApp/MyApp.xcodeproj` — a common layout when an app coexists with web/server code in the same repo). The 'apple' archetype's `[apple].project_path` field already expects a relative path, so the codebase is fine with nested layouts — only the detector is too strict.

Suggested fix: `rglob` with a small depth cap (2-3 dirs deep), then have the detector emit a hinted `[apple].project_path` based on what it found, so the user doesn't have to fill that in manually after bootstrap.

Saw this because: stash-reels has its Xcode project at `ios/StashReels/StashReels.xcodeproj`. Running `admin-gen --bootstrap --force .` against the repo logged \`detector matched: fallback\` and produced no apple archetype.

\`_detect_pkg_manager\` in \`admin_lib/web_dev.py\` checks for \`bun.lockb\` (the binary lockfile from Bun <1.0):

\`\`\`python
def _detect_pkg_manager(frontend_dir):
    if os.path.exists(os.path.join(frontend_dir, "bun.lockb")):
        return "bun"
    return "npm"
\`\`\`

Bun ≥1.0 uses \`bun.lock\` (plain text) instead of \`bun.lockb\`. Projects that have migrated or were initialized with a modern Bun release will fall through to \`npm\`, silently using the wrong package manager.

Fix: check for both filenames:

\`\`\`python
def _detect_pkg_manager(frontend_dir):
    for name in ("bun.lockb", "bun.lock"):
        if os.path.exists(os.path.join(frontend_dir, name)):
            return "bun"
    return "npm"
\`\`\`

install.sh has no uninstall counterpart. Also doesn't clean up v1 templates/ from prior installs at ~/.admin/templates/.

- Add uninstall.sh that removes ~/.admin/{admin_lib,templates,init-admin,init-admin-v2,bundle,gen,archetypes,detectors,VERSION}
- install.sh should rm -rf $DEST_DIR/templates when the v1 templates/ directory is deleted from the repo (cutover in #57)
